ue "images/bb/bb1554a6e02728076dbaf90e02aba2f87f6bfa33309a7da9060740da92b5fcf3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509834} {:answer/id #uuid "56cd32a0-fad3-576e-9ba0-52fba4bd4ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ed/ed5b0908aee7c2a2fbf065087ff2b09df5294b83c986e2d325489aba2eee3459.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509867} {:answer/id #uuid "574b2518-c168-5aa4-a98f-c7376cd2c3f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d366405b4fd522a8edaf6e2cf82eb7b97e6dc6869439b8035e55b6631ba4dced.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509870} {:answer/id #uuid "70d220ae-db4e-58c0-bc4a-b01f0765dde4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f0/f0ed0a1903d642e78d103d17a3fb309af76c6f792c3a9244b3c24607f165899f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a23b7a2-f1f6-520e-ad41-1ab5c9c5c23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cf/cfcee1a944e477bd909ef749d8d5d8967176340c359c664f0a97c887db5ab82d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509739} :answer-field/id #uuid "760e2ee6-413b-5589-acb9-b8d03aa02863" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa100519-5f40-5eb3-8aa6-b2668b120fa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-118283" :question/problem "![](images/39/392fab62a445326d26f7c637735cb03f13d94139ec0141d1802c8617020b1489.png)\n\nConsider the vector $a,$ shown above. Which of the following could be $a+(-a)?$" :question/worked-solution "According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $-a.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain a new vector for which the tail and head is the same point, the tail of $a.$ \n\nThat vector is called the zero vector, and we write\n\n$$\na+(-a)=0.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/96/96172072cf76df18a675eb506207756e65b7458e2f3c5fa056f54a81335fc6de.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "711d0e70-a248-5f93-a836-43bed5435d4f" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Two Vectors Using the Triangle Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32cf3ae7-e0ab-587b-b543-788e926bdf9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a5/a504ce78e5701a958f4a787bb1d2ed3a3d324027c992f8549085b68910216946.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509797} {:answer/id #uuid "4a337005-76c4-5a52-8411-24dfc17a2ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f9ea26f5540fbd4d5486bcd0e3cb810b167b160b4f612a51b781b8433d5573b0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509839} {:answer/id #uuid "a53d4220-b392-5cd3-80ab-9ad8d6ddf03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/56120a02f93b94c08baa445f22b34ef290165ce02609f25eb50e52a472c0db24.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510033} {:answer/id #uuid "b13f7bba-eb3e-5e0c-bbc0-77b62c492c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f55985250120af1277bc64d7e9b25215ae16b1a3cbffb21f98647b5617788c4c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510068} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf72d52-c34d-592d-91cc-ff5e4833cdbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/08/08adcd569189cfa3ecc99ab4bc6f7ecde7fb1f0b9bb4be54978865a4dfc972b4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdf72d52-c34d-592d-91cc-ff5e4833cdbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/08/08adcd569189cfa3ecc99ab4bc6f7ecde7fb1f0b9bb4be54978865a4dfc972b4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510234} :answer-field/id #uuid "af40cf27-ae86-54b2-948f-89455e9c5039" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6578d74-834c-5f37-879c-4ad4b226d0f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-118284" :question/problem "![](images/98/98619223439f3dbbb12f7849bfdb787ef952245569c16e7edf59b07ef908abd0.png)\n\nThe diagram shows the vectors $a$ and $b.$  Which of the following diagrams illustrates the vector subtraction $a-b.$" :question/worked-solution "We interpret the subtraction\n$a-b$\nas the addition\n\n$$\na+(-b),\n$$\n\nwhere $-b$ is the vector that has the same magnitude as $b$ but goes in the direction *opposite* of $b.$\n\nFinally, we use the triangle law to add the vectors $a$ and $-b:$ \n\n- We can start $a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane.\n\n- Next, we draw the vector that is equal to $-b$ and has its tail placed at the head of $a.$\n\n- Now, according to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $-\\text{b}$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/09/0990751c1d413600cba164bd50b732742b73ccc8bc0bcf3a3c039bc3693d8d5f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "711d0e70-a248-5f93-a836-43bed5435d4f" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting Two Vectors Using the Triangle Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "536b7056-cf83-5b72-abab-db8c3a002129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dceca1f109a6377db0877e6ccb1c0e950a3288cc7953757884f6ea16e9c21467.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509862} {:answer/id #uuid "5ef4d82a-905f-5ae8-9b37-4644e9232ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f2/f26c0030cd9d17197218ceb6d639edc5ff85ae93c20624ad67f66eefc1ff9e8c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509886} {:answer/id #uuid "61b62ed2-e6fa-508e-be46-05972095da9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2a/2a25a65f2ec4cc43a53051f739b999a55e807c509bc74c97852c837ea09a33db.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509892} {:answer/id #uuid "742051e9-131c-51fe-a81d-a856798f59c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9a/9a5dc1c9f479702ef746df13ca445b3fea68e0452e36e51ddff2622a19f24a84.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509932} {:answer/id #uuid "7f187e8d-d99b-5d1e-af89-9dce1640528d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b660479554e1f8f9a7106e0bc949eac8a97cd06ac676479ec38ef119f454973d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "742051e9-131c-51fe-a81d-a856798f59c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9a/9a5dc1c9f479702ef746df13ca445b3fea68e0452e36e51ddff2622a19f24a84.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509932} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2c501f0-31c4-5fe0-aad9-a91029b26492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6d8718b0-c85d-5066-80fb-cb2a1380aab6" :question/math-academy-id "q-118289" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bb7d3c1f1cf1ed19c22bad9eefc9f8c4911d70ed74231c5d63ed88a6cd710a67.png)\n\nThe diagram shows the vectors $a$ and $b.$  Which of the following diagrams illustrates the vector subtraction $-a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "We interpret  $-a+b$ as the addition\n\n$$\n(-a)+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $-a$ is the vector that has the same magnitude as $a$ but goes in the direction *opposite* of $a.$\n\nFinally, we use the triangle law to add the vectors $-a$ and $b:$ \n\n- We can start $-a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane.\n\n- Next, we draw the vector that is equal to $b$ and has its tail placed at the head of $-a.$\n\n- Now, according to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $-\\text{a}$ to the head of $\\text{b}$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c2/c21de8788e5808a48d725252c6308e817b756ca20cc6bbe0446fbfc124440c58.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096646 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9ae0161-d016-5aef-8c11-020047c66bbd" :knowledge-point/title "Adding More Than Two Vectors Using the Triangle Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2292cb83-da06-5374-8569-708024b1dd67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/28/28fc327298fb61bcd4140abb1c74bd4749efe0c339cf411afe4b99ce4c07400c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509759} {:answer/id #uuid "3f699177-2c7e-5534-8699-7c3f00a58bdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d8/d82556efc5965f68de5d68663ab6a60d7dac94a3d1b49b9cd8ee306fad38f105.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509824} {:answer/id #uuid "665a5698-611b-5436-bcea-96432be92280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/12/122df7ad9d20a94049597c1a75adf75f8286b7e67ca9b9a661029e21fea6393c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509901} {:answer/id #uuid "7a1f03d1-fdc7-5f23-9f51-0b77b3e898bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9dba0cd378e980b7f6935a8db01aa1e4338630926146df217e7e17d282fd39d4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509947} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7dd4b9-2650-576f-ab1b-cd43c6a18f9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/17/17cf4643da768e10a7c71107d5092d4a8ff3eb9628782765571bd3ab9fe2de16.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "665a5698-611b-5436-bcea-96432be92280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/12/122df7ad9d20a94049597c1a75adf75f8286b7e67ca9b9a661029e21fea6393c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509901} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffad1de5-4c55-5caf-87c3-832fe971927a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa07fa75-e006-5c8d-9bd3-e38658b1ba33" :question/math-academy-id "q-118546" :question/problem "![](images/92/926161e90964be4d6d4d32491ce4b6fdfa7e964d5d88ebc4eb7dd367dd2a837f.png)\n\nThe vectors $\\text{a},$ $\\text{b},$ and $\\text{c}$ are shown in the diagram above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $a-b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\na-b=a+(-b).\n$$\n\nThe resultant $a-b$ is the vector that joins the tail of $\\text{a}$ and the head of $-\\text{b}:$\n\n![](images/a4/a487c6406c591962ce27be6c27006c2d8f2ef49d05ee704007d578788db77883.png)\n\nNow, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\n(\\text{a}-\\text{b})+\\text{c}.\n$$\n\nWe draw $\\text{c}$ from the head of $\\text{a}-\\text{b}.$ So, we have the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $\\text{c}:$\n\n![](images/12/122df7ad9d20a94049597c1a75adf75f8286b7e67ca9b9a661029e21fea6393c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48176a87-796e-5637-9552-4f7fccdeee6a" :knowledge-point/title "Adding Two Vectors Using the Triangle Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eeb7bc9-4bd1-5041-aa09-30f7a26c0479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/93/936390d11842df6737547cd288ca042d46d84aed90597b1c1c1acb437ff36cd6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509821} {:answer/id #uuid "48bfe2e4-ef3c-5766-8c72-e82231567f72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d2/d24f6788e4c32eda66bf9994db7f6adcb7ef9bbfc945f420c8c29c1f13a0317a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509835} {:answer/id #uuid "48e4bf94-7608-5f05-ba8e-4f103e2ad95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/23/23f1536da00e8165b72a910c08cf3cabf48f725967986cc276832fcbb45db6d6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509836} {:answer/id #uuid "7d58d05f-acc8-5fcd-90ab-d63912486d64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52e0588ac90168749ada243bde475c5539cc3c04207f7c82ebbabf1601c380f3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509958} {:answer/id #uuid "9eaa0169-2290-598b-b3c1-3ffc1f80396e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5be467b02743825fcc1d67dcad5d6bd0743bdb43ff5900ca90f87f33fe0989ad.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9eaa0169-2290-598b-b3c1-3ffc1f80396e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5be467b02743825fcc1d67dcad5d6bd0743bdb43ff5900ca90f87f33fe0989ad.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510018} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5de92a1-ca0f-564f-9f85-876915ec1067" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f374050f-4aee-5c4e-89b5-51002237ae2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-69451" :question/problem "![](images/77/7711469c806f738c8dab65ded