12af-569c-b701-32bc6eb0c259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/955d3bed564303d79a3047310df139fce20ad698cc45c0c353f53608f2c1e57c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509752} {:answer/id #uuid "320b3562-cbad-56db-a302-8849208fccef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/597d3779c6748c4c96b9b43e30751f8443031091bb015048cc56a3fa8d04cf6f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509793} {:answer/id #uuid "326c84ac-e8aa-52e0-9dc1-13238a3daa00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4e/4e131814caab231af9390de4443f281bea8179fd07b61a08b8931062a735a1ca.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509794} {:answer/id #uuid "35b2ecbb-8412-549e-8ee4-b7b2ac3428dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/47/478de116b8b2364cc324046da2a102e1ff159d99bdfdd517ed26d75864bd6d33.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bf8e4cf-c0f3-551b-abbb-fb80164ac96f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/da/da52e611ffe7002e478024073ec134e4f5b6a6d1b12f19513fed24a0b03ba25b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509715} :answer-field/id #uuid "025afa14-11d3-50a3-94aa-2f8842d9174c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d8517d92-ae69-5efd-a845-0b2600987e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-69482" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6f1af14d60c9b2353d3aa149c4f74ead097289fd2a619013f1506cb783b72ee2.png)\n\nThe vectors $\\text{a},$ $\\text{b},$ and $\\text{c}$ are shown in the diagram above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $a-b-c.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\na-b=a+(-b).\n$$\n\nThe resultant $a-b$ is the vector that joins the tail of $\\text{a}$ and the head of $-\\text{b}:$\n\n![](images/40/40912329e0fa213a0bb8be143ed2d44441634ced3eaf378d76a69aa3167fe14c.png)\n\nNow, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\n(\\text{a}-\\text{b})-\\text{c}=(\\text{a}-\\text{b})+(-\\text{c}).\n$$\n\nWe draw $-\\text{c}$ from the head of $\\text{a}-\\text{b}.$ So, we have the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $-\\text{c}:$\n\n![](images/6c/6cbd0e043e9de98da0044792d5be99df0e1a17eff3b9dc8b87093985c5a27f24.png)"}]}
